{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019foShQTdAiAR66CmfNYBC8","type":"tool_result","content":"# Handover — 2026-05-19\n\n> 由 Agent 生成，每次状态变更后自动更新。硬限 150 行。\n\n## 运行中\n（无）\n\n## 待处理\n（无）\n\n## 近期结论\n- **phase2_4way_eval** (success): Turn-residual gating (TRG) improves multi-turn response quality over LoRA-only and base model baselines because it selectively amplifies conversational context signals, which should manifest as higher GAR scores across 4 conditions (base, base+TRG, LoRA, LoRA+TRG). ← 基于 phase2_tg_s42_v7\n- **phase2_lora_only_s42** (success): LoRA-only baseline (gate 固定 1.0，无 gating 机制) 在相同 MSE+NTP loss 下 GAR 应低于 ThreadGate (v7)。如果 LoRA-only 也能训到 GAR~0.5，则 gating 机制贡献为零，paper story 不成立。关键对比：LoRA-only 的 GAR 收敛值 vs v7 的 0.48。 ← 基于 phase2_tg_s42_v7\n- **phase2_ug_s42** (success): Uniform gating baseline: per-layer independent gates without turn conditioning (content-dependent only), to isolate whether ThreadGate's turn-conditioned gating provides benefit over content-only residual scaling. Same training setup as v7 but with gate-type=uniform. ← 基于 phase1_gar_diag\n\n## 趋势\n成功 6 / 负向 4 / 失败 1 / 共 12\ntraining_time_hours: 5.7 ↓（近 3 次 success）\ntraining_time_seconds: 20588.6 ↓（近 3 次 success）\n\n## 下一步\n（无活跃 idea，请通过 ideas.md 添加）\n\n## 资源状态\nwestd-20861: 无 GPU 信息\n\n## 告警\n- phase2_tg_s42_v2: 已被终止 — unknown\n- phase2_tg_s42_v4: 训练失败 — unknown","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0137htqXCutSAwkbesZWxyJZ","session_id":"a2798eb8-f7f1-44c1-8b40-8064e4595dc1","uuid":"95df5943-54f5-42bc-a570-43e0fdde27d7","timestamp":"2026-05-19T13:53:56.950Z"}
