get)\n- `L_gate_div`: `F.relu(min_std - gate_std)` (enforces per-layer diversity, stops when std > min_std)\n- Combined: `L_total = L_NTP + λ_GAR · L_GAR + λ_div · L_gate_div`\n- Loss evolution (v1-v7): pairwise/cumulative → maximize → smooth_saturation → **MSE+gate_div (v7 success)**\n\n---\n\n### **5. Evaluation Scripts**\n\n**Primary Evaluation Scripts:**\n\n1. **`run_phase1_gar.py`** (9.2K)\n   - Computes GAR on untrained base model\n   - Built-in 5 test conversations (knowledge_qa, coding_help, creative_writing, math, roleplay)\n   - Outputs GAR per turn, relative drops\n\n2. **`eval_phase2_gar.py`** (26K) — Main comprehensive evaluation\n   - Loads trained checkpoints (ThreadGate + LoRA weights)\n   - Two GAR variants:\n     - **GAR-ours**: goal = {system prompt + first user turn}, response = {last token per assistant turn}\n     - **GAR-Dongre**: goal = {system prompt task tokens only}, response = {all response tokens}\n   - Computes per-query, per-layer, per-head GAR with visualization\n   - Outputs JSON results + matplotlib curves\n   - Usage: `python eval_phase2_gar.py --checkpoint-dir /root/turn_residual_gating/checkpoints/tg_s42 --gate-type threadgate --gar-variant dongre`\n\n3. **`eval_phase2_mtbench.py`** (12K)\n   - Evaluates MT-Bench multi-turn subset\n   - Dual metrics: GAR + perplexity\n\n4. **`eval_phase2_multiturn.py`** (9.5K)\n   - Tests custom multi-turn conversation sets\n   - Turn-level analysis\n\n5. **`compare_phase2.py`** (11K)\n   - Four-way comparison script\n   - Compares Base, TG, UG, LoRA-only across metrics\n\n---\n\n### **6. Gradient Analysis & Attention Visualization**\n\n**Gradient Conflict Analysis** (Completed 2026-05-19)\n- **File location:** `/logs/workers/worker_code_gradient_conflict_analysis_20260519T112257_result.json`\n- **Script deployed to:** `/root/turn_residual_gating/src/gradient_conflict_analysis.py` (awaiting execution)\n- **Analysis plan:**\n  - Load v7 checkpoint + LoRA weights\n  - For each ultrachat sample: backward NTP loss, then backward GAR loss separately\n  - Collect 28-layer gate parameter gradients\n  - Per-layer metrics: cosine similarity (NTP-GAR gradient direction) + magnitude ratio\n  - Expected findings: 67-79% of layers have opposite gradient directions, NTP gradient dominates 7.5-14.7x\n\n**Key Findings (from memory.md):**\n- **NTP-GAR gradient conflict:** cos_sim ranges -0.089 → -0.042 across epochs, indicating persistent opposition\n- **Magnitude dominance:** Ratio grows 7.5x (epoch 0) → 14.7x (epoch 2)\n- **Implication:** NTP loss overpowers GAR signal in gradient-based learning\n\n**Attention Heatmap Visualization Code** (Deployed 2026-05-19)\n- File: `/logs/workers/worker_code_attention_visualization_20260519T114246_result.json`\n- Compares 4 models × 3 conversations × 28 layers × 10 turns\n- Metrics:\n  - Base: mean goal attention = 0.0136, T1→T10 decay = 87.5%\n  - TG v7: mean goal attention = 0.0232, T1→T10 decay = 77.7% (only 9.8pp improvement, statistical noise)\n  - UG: mean goal attention = 0.0216, T1→T10 decay = 80.3%\n  - LoRA-only: mean goal attention = 0.0216, T1→T10 decay = 81.0%\n- **Conclusion:** Gating mechanism has zero incremental effect on attention decay pattern\n\n---\n\n### **7. Training & Turn Detection Utilities**\n\n**`turn_utils.py`** (8.3K)\n- **`get_turn_markers()`**: Auto-detects turn boundary tokens from chat template\n  - Supports ChatML format (`<|im_start|>`, `<|im_end|>`)\n  - Supports Llama-3 format (`<|start_header_id|>`, `<|eot_id|>`)\n  \n- **`detect_turn_boundaries()`**: Identifies all turn boundaries in a sequence\n  - Returns turn role (system/user/assistant), start/end positions, content spans\n  \n- **`build_turn_features()`**: Constructs turn-aware features for gating\n  - Computes per-token turn distance (steps since last boundary)\n  - Assigns turn indices\n\n**`train_phase2.py`** (15K)\n- Full training loop with:\n  - MultiTurnDataset (loads ultrachat_8k from disk)\n  - LoRA adapter (rank=16, applied to q_proj/v_proj)\n  - Dual loss optimization (NTP + GAR-mse + gate-div)\n  - Gradient accumulation (steps=8)\n  - Learning rate warmup + cosine decay\n  - Checkpoint saving every epoch\n  - Gate statistics logging\n\n---\n\n### **8. Data & Preprocessing**\n\n**Primary Training Data:**\n- `ultrachat_8k`: 8,000 multi-turn conversations\n- Format: messages list with system/user/assistant roles\n- Processing: Chat template applied → tokenized → turn boundaries detected → goal/response positions extracted\n- Train/val split: Used for training, eval data from standard_conversations (see below)\n\n**Standard Evaluation Conversations** (Created to fix confound, 2026-05-19)\n- File: `/root/turn_residual_gating/data/standard_conversations.json`\n- 5 system prompts × 10 conversations × 10 turns each\n- Generated by base model (pre-gating)\n- Used consistently across Phase 1 → Phase 2 to avoid confounding variables\n\n**Diagnostic Scripts:**\n- `generate_standard_conversations.py` (5.7K) — Creates fixed eval set\n- `diagnose_data_turns.py` (3.9K) — Analyzes turn structure in datasets\n- `convert_ultrachat_to_eval.py` (2.0K) — Converts UltraChat for evaluation\n\n---\n\n### **9. Experiment Plan & Registry**\n\n**Completed Experiments (5/14):**\n- ✅ plan_001: Phase 1 GAR degradation diagnosis (registry: `phase1_gar_diag`)\n- ✅ plan_002: ThreadGate v7 training (registry: `phase2_tg_s42_v7`)\n- ✅ plan_003: Uniform Gate ablation (registry: `phase2_ug_s42`)\n- ✅ plan_004: LoRA-only ablation (registry: `phase2_lora_only_s42`)\n- ✅ plan_005: Four-way eval (registry: `phase2_4way_eval`)\n\n**Completed Analysis Tasks:**\n- ✅ plan_006: Gradient conflict analysis (code deployed, execution pending)\n- ✅ plan_007: Attention heatmap visualization (code deployed, analysis complete)\n\n**Remaining Planned Experiments (9):**\n- plan_008: Held-out evaluation on unseen UltraChat data (2h GPU)\n- plan_009-013: Llama-3.1-8B cross-model validation suite (15h GPU)\n- plan_014: Downstream task sanity check (1h GPU)\n- **GPU budget remaining:** ~19h (single RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, ~2-3 days wall time)\n- **Deadline:** EMNLP 2026 ARR August cycle (2026-08-03), ~10.5 weeks\n\n---\n\n### **10. Key Insights & Root Causes (from Memory & Paper Framing)**\n\n**Central Finding: 30x Training-Inference GAR Distribution Shift**\n- Training GAR: 0.48 (v7 converged)\n- Inference GAR: 0.016 (on same model)\n- Gap magnitude: **30x**, not a measurement bug\n- Root cause: Teacher-forcing in training vs. autoregressive generation at inference creates fundamental distribution shift\n\n**Three Coupled Failure Mechanisms:**\n1. **Reverse Turn Conditioning (NF1):** 27/28 gate layers learn opposite logic (suppress early turns where GAR is high, become passive at late turns where intervention needed)\n2. **NTP-GAR Gradient Competition (NF2):** Gate parameters face conflicting gradients; NTP dominates 7.5-14.7x; GAR signal marginalized\n3. **Insufficient Gate Magnitude at Inference (NF3):** Final gates near identity (mean=0.93-0.98), providing only 2-7% residual attenuation—too weak to shift attention patterns\n\n**Why Gating Cannot Work (Theoretical):**\n- Uniform gating (content-only) preserves positional bias distribution via Cesaro matrix theory\n- Turn-conditioned gating requires proper training signal, but NTP loss prevents learning\n- Alternative losses (maximize, smooth_saturation, hinge_target) all suffer identity collapse or gradient vanishing\n\n---\n\n### **11. Code Quality & Reproducibility**\n\n**Well-Documented & Reproducible:**\n- All hyperparameters centralized in `config.py`\n- Clear argument parsing in training/eval scripts\n- Tokenizer-aware turn detection (ChatML vs Llama-3)\n- Checkpoint management (epoch-level + best-loss tracking)\n- JSON output for all results\n\n**Known Caveats (from memory.md):**\n- stdout buffering can delay diagnostics; match by `step=` not line position\n- Llama-3 requires special attention to cache paths (`/root/.cache/modelscope` vs HuggingFace cache)\n- PEP 668 system constraints on AutoDL servers require careful environment management\n\n---\n\n### **Summary Table**\n\n| Category | Key Details |\n|----------|------------|\n| **Model** | Qwen-2.5-7B-Instruct (frozen) + ThreadGate modules (trainable) |\n| **Architecture** | 28-layer gating with turn embeddings + LoRA rank-16 adapter |\n| **Training Data** | UltraChat-8k (8000 multi-turn conversations) |\n| **Metrics** | GAR (Goal Accessibility Ratio), PPL (perplexity), NTP loss |\n| **Main Results** | Training GAR 0.48 → Inference GAR 0.016 (30x gap); zero gating benefit vs baselines |\n| **Paper Type** | Mechanistic negative result (Findings-track target) |\n| **Target Venue** | EMNLP 2026 ARR, August cycle deadline 2026-08-03 |\n| **Must-Have** | Llama-3.1-8B cross-model validation (W1 risk mitigation) |\n| **Status** | MVP negative result validated; transitioning to Route B paper (distribution shift + mechanistic insights) |"}],"totalDurationMs":102650,"totalTokens":85955,"totalToolUseCount":31,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5410,"cache_read_input_tokens":76038,"output_tokens":4503,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5410},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":4503,"cache_read_input_tokens":76038,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5410,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":13,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":17,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
